---
title: "Filters"
description: "Narrow QQL retrieval and mutations with comparisons, text, nested payload, vector, and geo predicates."
sidebar:
  order: 3
---

`WHERE` describes *which points qualify*. It lowers to a Qdrant filter for REST,
gRPC, and edge execution. It is independent from `SHARD`, which is request
routing rather than access control.

## Compose scalar predicates

Predicates combine with `NOT`, `AND`, and `OR`; precedence is predicate → `NOT`
→ `AND` → `OR`. Add parentheses when a mixed condition should be obvious to the
reader.

{% qqlExample title="Comparisons, membership, and boolean logic" %}
```sql
QUERY TEXT 'search'
FROM docs
WHERE status = 'published'
  AND year BETWEEN 2024 AND 2026
  AND tags NOT IN ('archived', 'private')
  AND (score >= 0.7 OR featured = true)
LIMIT 10;
```
{% /qqlExample %}

| Predicate | Use it for |
|---|---|
| `=`, `>`, `>=`, `<`, `<=` | Scalar equality and range comparison |
| `BETWEEN`, `IN`, `NOT IN` | Inclusive ranges and membership sets |
| `IS NULL`, `IS EMPTY` | Missing or empty payload values |
| `MATCH`, `MATCH ANY`, `MATCH PHRASE` | Text payload matching |
| `HAS_VECTOR`, `VALUES_COUNT` | Vector presence and array cardinality |

## Match nested document data

Use `NESTED` when predicates must apply within the same object of a nested
payload array. This avoids accidentally matching `rating` from one review and
`verified` from another.

{% qqlExample title="Phrase and nested-payload matching" %}
```sql
QUERY TEXT 'quality'
FROM products
WHERE description MATCH PHRASE 'machine washable'
  AND NESTED('reviews', rating >= 4 AND verified = true)
LIMIT 20;
```
{% /qqlExample %}

## Filter geographic data

Geo predicates accept structured point and shape objects. Latitude, longitude,
radius, and polygon structure are validated before planning.

{% qqlExample title="Points within a radius" %}
```sql
QUERY TEXT 'coffee'
FROM places
WHERE location GEO_RADIUS {
  center: {lat: 52.52, lon: 13.405},
  radius: 1500.0
}
LIMIT 10;
```
{% /qqlExample %}

{% qqlExample title="A geographic bounding box" %}
```sql
QUERY TEXT 'museum'
FROM places
WHERE location GEO_BBOX {
  top_left: {lat: 52.54, lon: 13.36},
  bottom_right: {lat: 52.49, lon: 13.45}
}
LIMIT 10;
```
{% /qqlExample %}

{% aside type="caution" title="Routing is not isolation" %}
`SHARD 'acme'` selects a Qdrant shard key and never becomes a Qdrant filter.
For a tenant boundary, inject a trusted predicate with the host SDK. Use both
when you need a security boundary and targeted routing.
{% /aside %}

See [Multitenancy](/docs/guides/multitenancy/) for the host-side policy pattern.
